A||N||6||Ozzy||Still sluggish on top end...2.5L, 88 coupe||||5||
Z||000000||Ozzy||02-13-2000||03:42 AM||||O.K. My duck is up and rolling well again but it still seems to have an ittermittent problem in the upper rev range. It pulls out fairly well but you can feels something of a drop off in the power curve. ( Yeah I know...not a term that should be identified with the duck)<BR>Anyway, I've replaced the plugs,plug wires, O2 sensor, Map Sensor, checked all vacuum lines and repaired including hose clamps on the PCV line, ignition mod has tested good, crank sensor has been replaced, IAC replaced.<BR>I have the kit for the TBI but have not done it yet. I also bought a new injector and will install it tomorrow.<P>What about the EGR? Could it be leaking by or something? Since I've spent about a million bucks on every other small part why not it too?!!<P>Also, I've just recently bought an '84 2m4. The top end of the engine is considerably quieter than my coupe. 2m4 has 100k and coupe has 127k. Should the rockers be ajusted for slack even though it has hydraulic lifters? If the head is worn, will the head from the '84 bolt straight on the '88 motor?<P>Ozzy||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phaeton||02-13-2000||03:57 AM||||You have piqued my curiosity.  By 'quieter' head do you mean are getting rocker noise?  A hydraulic cam loose enough to tick on all valves has a considerable shorter duration than spec and would lose major amounts of top end.  But it's the lifter slamming full speed into the valve seat thats going to cause damage if allowed to continue.  Cams are supposed  to slow the valve down at the last moment and set it Gently on the seat.  Fast impacts try to stretch the valve and if it's an exhaust valve it welds the surfaces together making them pit when pulled back apart.   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wrench||02-13-2000||08:06 AM||||Check your fuel pump pressure. Mine was low and my top end suffered greatly. If your pump has over 100k change it or you will be left stranded. New pump from NAPA cost me less than 100 bucks. Improvement in performance was amazing. If your pressure is ok,(45+psi), then this may not be your problem.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ozzy||02-13-2000||12:40 PM||||I need to check the fuel pressure. I'm just really hoping that is not the problem 'cause I don't wanna change that sucker!!<P>The noise from the head is not ticking noise like lifters but sorta like rockers. <P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ozzy||02-13-2000||11:33 PM||||O.K gang...I'm pleased to announce that after rebuilding my TBI and replacing the injector, the car is running noticably better!! Hesitation gone and smooth pull all the way out to 5000 rpm. The new IAC has solved the idle problems. I think it's finally there...hell, there's almost nothing to replace.(knock on wood!) The throttle body was full of junk. I cleaned it thouroughly inside and out and reassembled it with attention on all gasket surfaces.<P>Hope it keeps on running this way for awhile!<P>Happy at last Ozzy!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||02-14-2000||07:41 AM||||Ozzy<BR>Sounds like you finally got everything together, now you will have move up to the V6s and start all over again.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ozzy||02-14-2000||07:19 PM||||Ugh! Puhleeeze...I am in no hurry to start getting familiar with another engine and it's 'Fiero quirks'. Besides, I don't HAVE to have tons of power. I just want whatever I have to function to the best of it's capabilities.<P>I do like the look of the '87 & '88 GT's though. If I can get this thing pretty much restored I may sell it later but my wife is pregnant with our first child, we are trying to buy a house and I run a construction project with 85 people on it so I don't get a lot of spare time lately!!!<P>Contented Ozzy!||||reg||13
